Subject: add a /run tier to the provider-ordering directory search
Source: downstream patch for enchant 2.8.2
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on the /run/enchant-2 path

enchant_get_conf_dirs() (lib/provider.c, generated from provider.vala)
built an ordered list of only two system directories:
PKGDATADIR/enchant-2 (the vendor tree, /usr/share/enchant-2) and
SYSCONFDIR/enchant-2. src/Makefile.am:21 and lib/Makefile.am:55 both
substitute SYSCONFDIR from $(sysconfdir), and the package manifest ran
./configure --prefix=/usr with no --sysconfdir, so autotools kept its
${prefix}/etc default and SYSCONFDIR/enchant-2 compiled to
/usr/etc/enchant-2: a path under the immutable /usr tree that a
machine owner can never write. The manifest now passes
--sysconfdir=/etc, which fixes that unreachable administrator tier,
but the directory list still had no /run entry, so a boot could not
supply a transient provider-ordering override.

enchant_broker_load_provider_ordering() (lib/broker.c) calls
enchant_get_conf_dirs() and walks the returned list in order, loading
every "enchant.ordering" file it finds with
enchant_broker_load_ordering_from_file(), which in turn calls
enchant_broker_set_ordering() for each "tag:ordering" line. That
function stores the entry with g_hash_table_insert() keyed by
language tag, and g_hash_table_insert() replaces the value already
stored for an existing key, so a directory read later in the list
overwrites the same tag read from a directory earlier in the list.
enchant_broker_load_ordering_from_file() also already treats a
missing file as routine: g_io_channel_new_file() reports it through
the G_FILE_ERROR domain, which the generated code catches, logs with
g_debug(), and returns from without touching the hash table or
raising an error. A missing /run/enchant-2 (or /etc/enchant-2)
directory is therefore silent under the pre-existing behavior, and
this patch does not change that.

This patch adds ENCHANT_RUNDIR ("/run/enchant-2") to
enchant_get_conf_dirs()'s returned list, positioned after the vendor
directory and before the administrator's SYSCONFDIR/enchant-2 entry.
Because later list entries win ties per the overwrite behavior above,
the resulting order (vendor, then /run, then administrator) lets the
administrator's entry for a given language tag beat the same tag read
from /run, which beats the vendor default; the per-user directory
from enchant_get_user_config_dir() keeps its unchanged position at
the end of the list, so it keeps overriding every system tier.

This patch does not install anything under /run/enchant-2:
ENCHANT_RUNDIR is only a compiled-in search path that this package
does not populate.
--- a/lib/provider.c
+++ b/lib/provider.c
@@ -39,6 +39,14 @@
 #include <gmodule.h>
 #include <gobject/gvaluecollector.h>
 
+/* Nex UAPI patch: enchant_get_conf_dirs() (below) has no directory for a
+ * boot-time override between the vendor tree and the administrator's
+ * SYSCONFDIR tree. ENCHANT_RUNDIR names that directory; see the patch
+ * header for the full rationale. */
+#ifndef ENCHANT_RUNDIR
+#define ENCHANT_RUNDIR "/run/enchant-2"
+#endif
+
 #if !defined(VALA_STRICT_C)
 #if !defined(__clang__) && defined(__GNUC__) && (__GNUC__ >= 14)
 #pragma GCC diagnostic warning "-Wincompatible-pointer-types"
@@ -346,6 +354,20 @@
 		conf_dirs = g_slist_append (conf_dirs, _tmp6_);
 #line 348 "provider.c"
 	}
+
+	/* Nex UAPI patch: add the /run tier between the vendor and
+	 * administrator directories so a boot can supply a transient
+	 * enchant.ordering override. enchant_broker_load_provider_ordering()
+	 * (broker.c) walks this list in order and loads every
+	 * "enchant.ordering" file it finds, and enchant_broker_set_ordering()
+	 * (also broker.c) calls g_hash_table_insert() for each one, so a
+	 * later directory in this list overwrites an earlier directory's
+	 * entry for the same language tag. Putting ENCHANT_RUNDIR ahead of
+	 * the administrator's SYSCONFDIR tier below keeps the administrator
+	 * tier's entries as the final system word, matching the existing
+	 * vendor-then-administrator precedent this patch extends. */
+	conf_dirs = g_slist_append (conf_dirs, g_strdup (ENCHANT_RUNDIR));
+
 #line 50 "provider.vala"
 	_tmp7_ = _vala_gnulib_relocate (SYSCONFDIR);
 #line 50 "provider.vala"
